Support static export for GoDaddy hosting

Adds `npm run build:static`, which exports the whole site to ./out as
plain files for upload to GoDaddy cPanel or any static host. The normal
`npm run build` is untouched, so a Node host stays an option.

The mode is detected from the npm script name rather than an env var, so
it behaves the same on Windows and macOS without adding cross-env.

trailingSlash is on for the export so /privacy emits as
privacy/index.html, which Apache serves without MultiViews or rewrites.

The three generated routes needed `dynamic = "force-static"`; without it
output: export fails outright on /opengraph-image.

Adds public/.htaccess, which Next copies into the export. The important
line is the ForceType on "opengraph-image": Next exports the share card
with no file extension, so Apache would serve it as
application/octet-stream and every link preview would come out with no
image. Also forces HTTPS, wires the 404 page, caches hashed assets
immutably while keeping HTML uncached, and sets basic security headers.

